#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186352604 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e66d7cf-1a4b-51e6-9c78-f70a8c0555df" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Three Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa2b3f7f-9702-5246-a91c-8244aaf2c133" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{(3x+1)}+\\frac{3}{(x-4)}+\\frac{2}{(3-x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352606} {:answer/id #uuid "32f2ecf6-693f-5472-9688-c051e17ab82e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{(3x+1)}+\\frac{2}{(x-4)}+\\frac{5}{(3-x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352607} {:answer/id #uuid "b5a2ace9-b2aa-5626-9894-b95fadd8ef7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{(3x+1)}+\\frac{1}{(x-4)}+\\frac{4}{(3-x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352608} {:answer/id #uuid "7a6fd77d-307c-5f09-8de7-f5315fd229bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{(3x+1)}+\\frac{7}{(x-4)}-\\frac{3}{(3-x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352609} {:answer/id #uuid "43eda019-39d6-590b-9a4c-71d13d5c4649" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{(3x+1)}+\\frac{1}{(x-4)}+\\frac{5}{(3-x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352610}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa2b3f7f-9702-5246-a91c-8244aaf2c133" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{(3x+1)}+\\frac{3}{(x-4)}+\\frac{2}{(3-x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352606} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb7570c7-6938-506e-8bc1-464a98f80f24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352605}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c1c333d-3dc5-5692-88bb-2b4bd5c9dd8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-102531" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{37-19x}{(3x+1)(x-4)(3-x)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{37-19x}{(3x+1)(x-4)(3-x)} & =\\frac{A}{(3x+1)}+\\frac{B}{(x-4)}+\\frac{C}{(3-x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(3x+1)(x-4)(3-x)$ gives\n\n$$\n37-19x=A(x-4)(3-x)+B(3x+1)(3-x)+C(3x+1)(x-4).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{1}{3}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}37-19(-\\frac{1}{3}) & =A(-\\frac{1}{3}-4)(3-(-\\frac{1}{3})) \\\\  & +B(3(-\\frac{1}{3})+1)(3-(-\\frac{1}{3})) \\\\  & +C(3(-\\frac{1}{3})+1)(-\\frac{1}{3}-4) \\\\ 37+\\frac{19}{3} & =A(-\\frac{130}{9}) \\\\ \\frac{130}{3} & =A(-\\frac{130}{9}) \\\\ A & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=4$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}37-19(4) & =A(4-4)(3-4) \\\\  & \\,+B(3(4)+1)(3-4) \\\\  & +C(3(4)+1)(x-4) \\\\ 37-76 & =B(-13) \\\\ B & =\\frac{-39}{-13} \\\\ B & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=3$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}37-19(3) & =A(3-4)(3-3) \\\\  & \\,+B(3(3)+1)(3-3) \\\\  & +C(3(3)+1)(3-4) \\\\ 37-57 & =C(-10) \\\\ C & =\\frac{-20}{-10} \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{37-19x}{(3x+1)(x-4)(3-x)}=-\\frac{3}{(3x+1)}+\\frac{3}{(x-4)}+\\frac{2}{(3-x)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186352611 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e66d7cf-1a4b-51e6-9c78-f70a8c0555df" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Three Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b70e43cc-0951-5852-b1d9-ba90140fdbda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352613} {:answer/id #uuid "5d39504e-c749-50e9-abc7-953cf5099c9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352614} {:answer/id #uuid "ded53c14-7e84-5053-b110-3d2aa93f2ee0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352615} {:answer/id #uuid "f33809b4-71f1-514e-98fb-e269a5e47a96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352616} {:answer/id #uuid "1841c009-fbb3-5600-bf21-e2891daeabbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d39504e-c749-50e9-abc7-953cf5099c9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352614} :answer-field/id #uuid "e16b8340-c9f5-593e-86bb-f3b46127b46a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352612}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fd342860-f742-5a8f-909b-f28adb96df95" :question/math-academy-id "q-102540" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{x}^{2}+7x-24}{(x+2)(x-1)(x+4)}=\\frac{A}{(x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)}+\\frac{C}{(x+4)},\n$$\n\nwhere $A,$ $B$ and $C$ are real constants, calculate $A+B+C.$" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{x}^{2}+7x-24}{(x+2)(x-1)(x+4)}=\\frac{A}{(x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)}+\\frac{C}{(x+4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x+2)(x-1)(x+4)$ gives\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}+7x-24=A(x-1)(x+4)+B(x+2)(x+4)+C(x+2)(x-1).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-2,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-2)^{2}+7(-2)-24 & =A(-2-1)(-2+4) \\\\  & \\,+B(-2+2)(-2+4) \\\\  & \\,+C(-2+2)(-2-1) \\\\ -30 & =A(-6) \\\\ A & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=1,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{(1)}^{2}+7(1)-24 & =A(1-1)(1+4) \\\\  & \\,+B(1+2)(1+4) \\\\  & \\,+C(1+2)(1-1) \\\\ 2+7-24 & =B(15) \\\\ -15 & =15B \\\\ B & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-4,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-4)^{2}+7(-4)-24 & =A(-4-1)(-4+4) \\\\  & \\,+B(-4+2)(-4+4) \\\\  & \\,+C(-4+2)(-4-1) \\\\ 32-28-24 & =C(10) \\\\ -20 & =C(10) \\\\ C & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B+C & =5+(-1)+(-2)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186352618 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "450aebfe-d896-50bc-a392-e43aee7afabd" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Two Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38c1aade-2616-5000-ac73-04a93d580f66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352620} {:answer/id #uuid "4daa0931-31d7-5ab4-a6fb-462f00f60b46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352621} {:answer/id #uuid "1a9be564-cbc3-55cb-be20-6c7f79260e3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352622} {:answer/id #uuid "54f1ed97-cd7c-5200-9d36-8e448b00e78b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352623} {:answer/id #uuid "a2a13ebd-bdc0-53c9-b447-6d3793c82ec4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352624}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a9be564-cbc3-55cb-be20-6c7f79260e3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352622} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a12fa94-a4f7-5c95-a86a-284e6b352747" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352619}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8d3fa7d-1af4-572c-b501-d21a0a4e3c46" :question/math-academy-id "q-10957" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{13}{(3x+2)(2x-3)}=\\frac{A}{(3x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(2x-3)},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants, calculate $A+B.$" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{13}{(3x+2)(2x-3)}=\\frac{A}{(3x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(2x-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(3x+2)(2x-3)$ gives\n\n$$\n13=A(2x-3)+B(3x+2).\n$$\n\nFor $x=\\frac{3}{2}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13 & =A(2(\\frac{3}{2})-3)+B(3(\\frac{3}{2})+2) \\\\ 13 & =B(\\frac{9+4}{2}) \\\\ B & =\\frac{26}{13} \\\\ B & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{2}{3}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13 & =A(2(\\frac{-2}{3})-3)+B(3(-\\frac{2}{3})+2) \\\\ 13 & =A(\\frac{-13}{3}) \\\\ A & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nA+B=-3+2=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186352625 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "450aebfe-d896-50bc-a392-e43aee7afabd" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Two Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c1b7001-f05e-5f69-a85b-36ed2d16562a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c1b7001-f05e-5f69-a85b-36ed2d16562a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352627} :answer-field/id #uuid "6327db0d-a77b-59b2-9997-d5b833a92009" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352626} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21bd4e48-1eb7-5539-91a4-eb9c7000720b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21bd4e48-1eb7-5539-91a4-eb9c7000720b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352629} :answer-field/id #uuid "909aeb4e-86a5-50f9-b458-6b0eb2bc601d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352628}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "acaa0dd2-82c8-5290-93c1-72f9233435d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-346793" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{4x+23}{(5-2x)(x+3)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{4x+23}{(5-2x)(x+3)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $5-2x$ |  | $x+3$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{4x+23}{(5-2x)(x+3)}=\\frac{A}{5-2x}+\\frac{B}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(5-2x)(x+3)$ gives\n\n$$\n4x+23=A(x+3)+B(5-2x).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-3$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(-3)+23 & =A(-3+3)+B(5-2(-3)) \\\\ 11 & =11B \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=\\frac{5}{2},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(\\frac{5}{2})+23 & =A(\\frac{5}{2}+3)+B(5-2(\\frac{5}{2})) \\\\ 33 & =A(\\frac{11}{2}) \\\\ A & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{4x+23}{(5-2x)(x+3)}=\\frac{6}{5-2x}+\\frac{1}{x+3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186352630 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "450aebfe-d896-50bc-a392-e43aee7afabd" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Two Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbd85d44-3f79-5859-8a53-e18c04464541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbd85d44-3f79-5859-8a53-e18c04464541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352632} :answer-field/id #uuid "fecfee07-e547-55f2-b75f-d6ec657981d9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352631} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7908fadf-138e-5f7b-9d2c-892d7973481f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7908fadf-138e-5f7b-9d2c-892d7973481f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352634} :answer-field/id #uuid "405a34f4-4418-541f-b93f-b390cdc7778d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352633}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "022bf2da-ce27-5d90-8966-2809e6a6cd28" :question/math-academy-id "q-350950" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{4x-1}{(x+1)(2x-3)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{4x-1}{(x+1)(2x-3)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x+1$ |  | $2x-3$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{4x-1}{(x+1)(2x-3)}=\\frac{A}{x+1}+\\frac{B}{2x-3}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x+1)(2x-3)$ gives\n\n$$\n4x-1=A(2x-3)+B(x+1).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-1$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(-1)-1 & =A(2(-1)-3)+B(-1+1) \\\\ -5 & =-5A \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=\\frac{3}{2},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(\\frac{3}{2})-1 & =A(2(\\frac{3}{2})-3)+B(\\frac{3}{2}+1) \\\\ 5 & =\\frac{5}{2}B \\\\ B & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{4x-1}{(x+1)(2x-3)}=\\frac{1}{x+1}+\\frac{2}{2x-3}.\n$$"}]}
